UPDATE companies SET description='Magna-Power Electronics was founded in 1981 in Flemington, New Jersey, where it maintains a vertically integrated manufacturing headquarters. The company designs and builds programmable DC power supplies and electronic loads, controlling the entire production process from sheet metal fabrication and machining to printed circuit board assembly and final test.

The facility houses CNC vertical and horizontal machining centers, wire EDM, robotic bonded-fin heat-sink assembly, SMT lines with a Europlacer stencil printer and IINEO pick-and-place, two through-hole insertion lines, and 14 assembly stations for wire harnessing and sub-assembly. Magna-Power reports more than 250,000 available configurations spanning 1.5 kW to 10,000 kW+, with over 475 MW of product shipped and 50,000 units delivered to date. Typical made-to-order build time is four to six weeks.

Customers range from startups to Fortune 500 companies across aerospace, defense, academic research, robotics, and energy sectors. Named references include GE Aviation, Lockheed Martin, QinetiQ, Blue Robotics, Alencon Systems, and universities such as the University of Houston, George Washington University, and Colorado School of Mines.

The company attributes its differentiation to vertical integration, which gives it control over quality, cost, and lead times, and to co-locating engineering with manufacturing to foster continuous improvement. A large inventory of common assemblies supports made-to-order delivery, while unified firmware, SCPI commands, and standard options such as high slew rate, integrated blocking diode, water cooling, and the DBx module simplify integration across product families.', certifications=ARRAY['CE Mark']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC vertical machining (wet/dry)", "CNC horizontal machining for high-voltage insulators", "Wire EDM", "Precision brazing and fabrication for water-cooled magnetics and liquid-piping systems", "Custom shunt fabrication for precision current sensing", "Powder coating (iron phosphate wash, masking, electrostatic spray, bake)", "Metal sanding for deburring and powder coating prep", "Wood-working for custom packaging fabrication", "Robotic bonded fin heat sink assembly", "SMT assembly (Europlacer stencil printer, IINEO pick and place)", "Through-hole insertion lines for power components", "Wire harnessing and preparation", "Sub-assembly (14 assembly stations)", "Internally developed wire harness boards", "Programmable DC power supply design and manufacture", "DC electronic load design and manufacture", "Firmware and software development (SCPI, LabVIEW, IVI drivers)", "High slew rate output option", "Integrated blocking diode option", "Water cooling option", "DBx Module high-performance option"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Academic Research", "Robotics", "Energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Europlacer stencil printer", "IINEO pick and place", "CNC vertical machining centers (wet/dry)", "CNC horizontal machining centers", "Wire EDM", "Robotic bonded fin heat sink assembly", "Two through-hole insertion lines", "Fourteen assembly stations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4-6 weeks for made-to-order builds", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated USA manufacturing under one roof", "Complete control over quality, cost, and lead times", "Industry-leading made-to-order build times of 4\u20136 weeks", "Consistent firmware, commands, and features across all product families", "Substantial investment in stocked common assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 -> /", "Headquarters Flemington, New Jersey -> /", "Vertically integrated manufacturing -> /", "Products: programmable DC power supplies and electronic loads -> /", "475+ MW products shipped -> /", "250,000+ available configurations -> /", "50,000+ products delivered -> /", "Typical build-time 4-6 weeks -> /", "CNC vertical/horizontal machining, wire EDM -> /", "Europlacer stencil printer, IINEO pick and place -> /", "Two through-hole insertion lines -> /", "14 assembly stations -> /", "Robotic bonded fin heat sink assembly -> /", "Powder coating, metal sanding, wood-working -> /", "Precision brazing, custom shunt fabrication -> /", "Customers: GE Aviation, Lockheed Martin, QinetiQ, Blue Robotics, Alencon Systems, University of Houston, George Washington University, Colorado School of Mines -> /", "CEMARK certification -> db", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Magna-Power Electronics designs and manufactures its products at its vertically integrated headquarters in Flemington, New Jersey.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='magna-power-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Magnum Electronics, Inc., a family-owned communications systems integrator, is headquartered in Dover, Delaware. The company focuses on supporting mission-critical emergency workers in government and enterprise sectors.

Magnum supplies and services public-safety digital two-way radio systems, 4G LTE wireless networks, rugged mobile computers, and GPS fleet management solutions. As a Motorola Solutions Elite Channel Partner and Cradlepoint Partner, the firm designs custom wireless architectures spanning RF, LTE, and WiFi, handles FCC licensing, performs professional installation and vehicle upfitting, and provides factory-certified repair, programming, and bench service. It also offers short- and long-term radio rentals configured on nationwide FCC frequencies, and operates an AI-powered video telematics platform for real-time fleet tracking and driver safety monitoring.

The company holds State of Delaware contracts for equipment and installation and is an approved vendor for Delaware SB79 in-building public-safety coverage testing.

