ed"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='majors-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Maker Shop Boise operates a community woodworking facility in Boise, Idaho. The shop provides members and day-pass users with access to a range of professional-grade tools, a dedicated CNC room, and an epoxy room, all in a climate-controlled environment.

The facility runs on a membership model that includes free safety and operation training on all equipment. Members can use community workstations on a first-come, first-served basis, while the CNC room and epoxy room are reservable in advance. A day pass costs $99. The shop''s equipment roster includes an Axiom AR8 Pro V5 CNC router, along with a full suite of woodworking machinery that is maintained and sharpened by staff. No headcount or facility square footage is published.

The shop serves individual woodworkers, hobbyists, and makers rather than industrial clients. Customers range from beginners building birdhouses to experienced craftspeople constructing cabinets. The company emphasizes a supportive community where members can ask questions, share projects, and learn from mentors and peers.

Maker Shop Boise positions itself as a cost-effective alternative to owning a personal workshop. By bundling tool access, training, and space into a monthly membership, it aims to lower the barrier to entry for woodworking. The company highlights its climate-controlled shop, well-maintained tools, and free training as key differentiators that help users save time and money while building confidence.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woodworking tool access", "CNC routing (Axiom AR8 Pro V5)", "Epoxy room access", "Safety and operation training", "Woodworking classes", "Mentor-supported project guidance"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Axiom AR8 Pro V5 CNC"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free safety and operation training included with membership", "Climate-controlled facility with professionally maintained tools", "Membership includes access to full suite of woodworking equipment", "Community of mentors and peers for project support", "Day passes and classes available for non-members"], "facts_used": ["Location: Boise, Idaho -> db", "Day pass price $99 -> /", "Community workstations first-come first-served, CNC room and epoxy room reservable -> /", "Axiom AR8 Pro V5 CNC machine -> /", "Free safety & operation training included -> /", "More than 200 years collective mentor experience -> /", "Membership includes full suite of tools -> /", "Climate-controlled facility -> /", "Serves woodworkers, hobbyists, makers -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Get access to quality tools, free training, and fun classes. Join the growing community of woodworkers", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maker-shop-boise' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mālama Solar is a locally owned and operated solar installation company based in Honolulu, Hawaii. Founded by Chris and Rachel Ah Sue, the business was built on the Hawaiian principle of mālama ‘āina—caring for the land so the land cares for you. The couple, who have deep roots in the islands, started the company to bring a transparent, customer-first approach to residential solar.

The company designs and installs photovoltaic systems and energy storage for homeowners across Oahu and the Big Island. Its five-step process covers an initial energy-usage consultation, custom system design, permitting and HOA coordination, installation (typically completed in two days after a 6–8 week lead time), and ongoing post-install support. Mālama Solar partners with manufacturers, distributors, and financial institutions to supply panels, batteries, and financing options, and it was named to the Inc. 5000 list of fastest-growing private companies.

Mālama Solar serves residential customers throughout Hawaii, including homeowners in Kona, Kapolei, and Ewa Beach who have reported monthly savings of hundreds of dollars on electric bills. The company also works with homeowners associations to ensure compliance during installation.

The founders say they created Mālama Solar to be different from other providers: they emphasize upfront transparency, a dedicated local crew, and a commitment to the community through cultural awareness events and the mālama ‘āina ethic.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Energy usage analysis", "Permitting and HOA approvals", "Solar panel installation", "Energy storage installation", "Financing arrangement", "Post-installation customer support"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Renewable energy", "Home energy storage"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Energy storage batteries"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6-8 weeks for installation after sign-up, sometimes as soon as 3 weeks; installation itself takes about 2 days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founders Chris and Rachel Ah Sue -> /about-us", "Headquarters Honolulu, Hawaii -> db and homepage", "Five-step process (consult, design, permits, installation, power on) -> /services", "Installation timeline 6-8 weeks, installation 2 days -> /services", "Inc. 5000 fastest-growing listing -> homepage", "Local crews on Oahu and Big Island -> homepage", "Partners with manufacturers for panels, storage, financing -> homepage", "M\u0101lama \u2018\u0101ina value and community focus -> /about-us", "Customer testimonials from Kona, Kapolei, Ewa Beach -> homepage"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Hawaii''s local solar panel installer on Oahu and Big Island", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='malama-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
