UPDATE companies SET description='Manual Woodworkers & Weavers was founded in 1932 by Tom Oates in Hendersonville, North Carolina, amid the region''s bustling textile industry. The privately owned company established itself in the mountains of western North Carolina as an innovative force in the gift and decorative accessories market.

The company designs and produces a broad range of decorative accessories, including pillows, throws, quilts, wall hangings, wind chimes, figurines, candles, and seasonal décor. Product lines span categories such as garden, nautical, lodge, western, Americana, and inspirational themes, often featuring artwork from licensed artists like Thomas Kinkade Studios, Nicky Boehme, and Lori Siebert.

MWW sells wholesale to retailers, florists, and gift shops, offering programs such as Manual Margin Makers and a presence on the Faire wholesale marketplace. The company also provides a store finder for end consumers and collaborates with a roster of artists to create branded collections.

