UPDATE companies SET description='Manufacturing Works operates from Laramie, Wyoming, where it was established in 2019 as the state''s designated NIST Manufacturing Extension Partnership (MEP) Center. The organization was created to help Wyoming manufacturers and producers of all sizes improve their competitiveness through customized support, technology adoption, and specialized services.

Rather than producing goods itself, Manufacturing Works delivers consulting and implementation services across eight core areas: continuous improvement, cybersecurity, advanced manufacturing technologies, ISO and quality management, prototyping, supply chain optimization, business excellence assessment, and workforce development and training. Its expertise extends to additive manufacturing implementation, AR/VR integration, automation planning, CRM/ERP deployment, IoT education, and Lean Six Sigma methodologies. The center matches services to each client through detailed assessments aimed at increasing efficiency, profitability, and reducing operational bottlenecks.

The center serves Wyoming-based manufacturers across diverse sectors. Documented clients include Integrated Well Services, Inc. in Sweetwater County, community makerspace Maker Space 307, STYP, LLC, Red River, LLC, TITUS Wastewater Solutions, and Pertech Industries, Inc. These engagements range from fabricating complex plastic parts to implementing training programs that create engineering career pathways.

Manufacturing Works states its mission is to "Power Wyoming''s manufacturing success through customized support, technology, and services." It positions itself as a catalyst for transitioning the state''s manufacturing base from Industry 2.0 and 3.0 to Industry 4.0, emphasizing technology adoption and workforce readiness as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Continuous Improvement", "Cybersecurity", "Advanced Manufacturing Technologies", "ISO & Quality Management", "Prototyping", "Supply Chain Optimization", "Business Excellence Assessment", "Workforce Development & Training", "Additive Manufacturing Implementation", "AR/VR Implementation", "Automation Planning and Implementation", "CRM/ERP Implementation", "Emerging Manufacturing Technologies Education", "Internet of Things (IoT) Education", "Lean and Six Sigma Implementation"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Wyoming''s designated NIST MEP Center", "Customized client assessments matching services to specific needs", "Focus on Industry 4.0 transition for Wyoming manufacturers", "Expertise in additive manufacturing, automation, AR/VR, IoT, and cybersecurity implementation", "Track record of helping clients create jobs, increase sales, and achieve cost savings"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2019 -> db", "Headquarters Laramie, Wyoming -> db", "Wyoming''s NIST MEP Center -> /about-us", "Mission: Power Wyoming''s manufacturing success through customized support, technology, and services -> /about-us", "Core services: Continuous Improvement, Cybersecurity, Advanced Manufacturing Technologies, ISO & Quality Management, Prototyping, Supply Chain Optimization, Business Excellence Assessment, Workforce Development & Training -> /services", "Expertise areas: Additive Manufacturing Implementation, AR/VR Implementation, Automation Planning and Implementation, CRM/ERP Implementation, Cybersecurity Implem